        "text": "The Justice Department has responsibility for pursuing prosecutions.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Congress's role in prosecution is limited to making referrals and documenting reasons for prosecution.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The Justice Department will be responsible for advancing the case through the criminal justice system.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "A 'lack' (likely meaning 'case') is ready to be pursued by the Justice Department.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The Justice Department is the appropriate and legitimate body to handle criminal prosecutions.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "There exists a formal mechanism for congressional referrals to initiate prosecutorial action.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The criminal justice system functions effectively when properly initiated by competent authorities.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker trusts the Justice Department’s ability and willingness to act on referrals.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "Prosecutorial decisions should follow established institutional roles rather than political influence.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 92681,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92681.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "you know, I'll tell you, I think that as soon as they do, It will have a great impact on other witnesses who will realize that if they try to ignore lawful requests for information, that they will be charged with a crime. And that to me is a much more powerful deterrent than anything we had in the last four years when people knew that they could tie us in court for years.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "As soon as they act, it will have a significant impact on other witnesses.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Other witnesses will realize that ignoring lawful requests for information may lead to criminal charges.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The threat of criminal prosecution serves as a stronger deterrent than previous measures.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "In the past four years, individuals were able to delay proceedings by tying the authorities in court for extended periods.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
