  {
    "episode_id": 92681,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92681.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "You know, at the moment they're engaging with our committee, and I can't go into the nature of that engagement, but if we reach the point where they simply refuse or we determine that it's a delay tactic. then we'll move forward with whatever remedies that we have. We were, for example, engaging with Jeffrey Clark, this former Justice Department official who allegedly was involved in trying to get Georgia or try to get the Justice Department to force Georgia to delay the appointment of electors or appoint more than one slate of electors. And when we concluded that we were getting nowhere with this Council, we move very quickly from voluntary compliance to subpoena and a legal demand for compliance. And similarly, where we subpoena people and we get the sense that they're they're stonewalling, then we will make appropriate finding and refer to the Justice Department.",
