    "turn_text": "our best, but it reveals a lot about who we are. Power revealed Bill Barr to be, be craven, be willing to do almost anything to be at the seat of power once again, including just deliberately mislead the country about what Bob Mueller has said in his report repeatedly. And when he was asked by Congress whether Mueller or his team had communicated their deep upset about his misrepresentations, he misrepresented the Congress. about those communications with Mueller. And I think in a way that, in the same way that Donald Trump, because he lies so constantly, believes that everyone else lies the way he does. Because he's corrupt, he views everyone else, must be corrupt in the same way. I think Bob Mueller, because he's a man of such great integrity and rectitude, presumed that others had the same rectitude. And I have to imagine that he was devastated by the duplicity of Bill Barr and his willingness to misrepresent two years above Mueller's work in order to serve the President's interests.",
