    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "I think that they need to investigate the President's crimes and the ones that I'm most concerned about, frankly, are ones that took place long after his obstruction of justice. In particular, Donald Trump on the phone to the Secretary of State of Georgia. trying to coerce that Secretary of State in defining 11,780 votes that don't exist, that he knows doesn't exist. And the fact that he gives such a specific number, just the number he would need to beat Biden, shows just how corrupt a demand this was. And I think anyone else who made that demand would have been indicted by now. And I just don't see any sign that's even being investigated.",
