    "turn_text": "maybe at the end of the day, you have to make a difficult decision about whether to prosecute a prior president. But I don't think you can just ignore the crimes that have been committed. And so I do think that these need to be vigorously investigated by the Justice Department. There's already an indictment in the Southern District of New York of someone named individual number one who we know to be Donald Trump. for directing and coordinating a campaign fraud scheme. The Justice Department argued that Michael Cohen needed to go to jail because he was directed and coordinated in that scheme. So what's the argument for saying that the guy that did the directing and did the coordinating somehow gets a pass. So, I mean, I think if we're going to hold to the principle that no one is above the law, that means Donald Trump too. You know, we've all heard the, you know, too big to fail argument about the banks. Are we now to assume that a president, no matter how corrupt is somehow too big to jail?",
