    "turn_idx": 36,
    "turn_text": "I think that these crimes need to be investigated. These alleged crimes need to be investigated. And, you know, again, I don't envy the difficulty of the judgment that the Attorney General would have to make once you work it up and you see what laws may have been violated. And then you do the balancing of how important it is, how strong the evidence it is, and yes, what impact that has on the country to to potentially jail a former president. But I don't think you ignore it. And I don't see any signs at this point that the Justice Department is even reviewing those actions. And that to me is dangerous. After the partner of Nixon, after four years of Trump in which the Justice Department said you can't prosecute him and still the president, to now say we can't even look at the criminal conduct he may have been engaged in. creates a very dangerous different precedent. And I just don't think that we can turn away from that in the interest of moving forward. I think in order to truly move forward, we need to have an accounting of what's taken place.",
