  {
    "episode_id": 92681,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92681.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 48,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, in terms of how I keep going. At times, I have to say, in the thick of it, I would say in the morning, I just need to get through the day. And at the end of the day, I would say with some marvel, I'm still standing. And I was determined to get up every morning and do the best I could to the best of my ability and realize that was all I could do. And I think everyone needs to realize they can't do everything. Don't be paralyzed into doing nothing because we can't do everything. There is a role for each one of us to play. And I wanted to write the stories, not just of those that capitulated to Trump's immorality, but more importantly to those who stood up to him. The people like former Ambassador to Ukraine were Yovanovitch and former Sharjah a Bill Taylor, Alexander Vinman, a purple harper recipient, who was questioned about his patriotism because he had the unmitigated to Marity to report. to the White House Council that he thought what the president was doing was wrong and maybe even worse than wrong, you know, the Fiona Hills, you know, Dan Coates, who was leading the intelligence community but wouldn't go along with presidents, lies about Russia or love affair with Kim Jong-un. You know,",
