  {
    "episode_id": 92681,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92681.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 63,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, thank you for the very kind words about the book. And in terms of how long it will take to prosecute, the first critical decision will be for the Justice Department to bring the case. And I would hope that they would make that decision quickly and bring charges quickly because there's a real urgency here to getting to the bottom of all those who were involved in that insurrection. Once they do charge deep-handed, they make an arrest. It's assigned to a judge. He is arraigned. I think all of that takes place fairly quickly once the case is initiated. It could be that when they bring it to the grand jury that they feel they need to do more investigation after bringing it to the grand jury to ultimately file charges, although frankly it seems to be pretty open and shut. But then it's That's a question of the court system. And the court system is because of the pandemic, pretty overwhelmed as a general matter. But I think that a case of this seriousness, hopefully both the prosecution and the court will understand the need for some urgency.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
