    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 92681,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92681.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 67,
    "turn_text": "I think your question is exactly right, and really part of our mission. We have subpoenaed a number of organizations that have documents that will help us determine, okay, who paid for this? Who organized this? Why were there different permits when there was a connection between the different organizations that were involved in the rallies that led up to the insurrection? What was the role of these white nationalist groups? Did these white nationalist groups that generally operate separate from each other? Did they coordinate and collaborate? Why did they know to bring military gear with them? So these are just some of the questions, frankly, some of the biggest questions involved the president. What did the president know about the likelihood of violence? What did the president know about the participation of white nationalist groups? What was the president's plan and expectation For January 6, if Mike Pence didn't do what he wanted him to do and refused to accept the certification of states that had voted for Joe Biden. So those questions are at the heart of what we're investigating. We're determined to get the answers.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
